From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:21:11 -0400
Subject: commandbar: open a command bar on Cmd+T

Cmd+T opens a floating command bar over the content instead of a bare new
tab: type to search open tabs across every Space, pick one to switch Space
and activate it, or enter a URL or query for a new tab. Styled to the
reference; a dev parameter (open_command_bar) opens it at startup for
captures.

The bar is a layered child of the browser window rather than a popup window
of its own: a popup on macOS is shown without becoming key, so keystrokes go
to the window behind it. Inside the window the field takes focus through the
window's focus manager, Escape is an accelerator on it, and focus leaving the
bar dismisses it.

Why: Cmd+T is the most-used key in a browser and the reference makes it the
way in to everything, including other Spaces.
Removable when: never, short of dropping the command bar. The surface colours
become theme ids once Stedding has its own tokens for floating surfaces.
